# 🌊 DWM — Dynamic Window Manager (v1)

![Arch Linux](https://img.shields.io/badge/Arch-Linux-1793d1?style=for-the-badge&logo=arch-linux&logoColor=white)
![C](https://img.shields.io/badge/C-00599C?style=for-the-badge&logo=c&logoColor=white)
![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Rice%20In%20Progress-green?style=for-the-badge)

*A heavily customized, minimal, storm-inspired maritime desktop environment built on Arch Linux.*

</div>

---

## ✨ Applied Patches

| Patch | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **📌 `attachbelow`** | Newly spawned windows open directly below the active window instead of stealing the master slot. |
| **🔄 `restartsig`** | Allows restarting `dwm` on the fly via keybinding or signal without dropping your X session. |
| **💾 `preserveonrestart`** | Maintains window state, workspace tags, and positions across window manager restarts. |
| **🎨 `pango`** | Enables rich font rendering, colors, and markup support inside the status bar. |
| **📏 `bar height / padding`** | Custom vertical and side padding for a sleek, floating status bar layout. |
| **🎯 `alwayscenter`** | Automatically forces floating windows to spawn dead-center on the monitor. |
| **🖱️ `resizehere`** | Enables smooth mouse-based window resizing from any point on the window. |
| **📐 `vanitygaps`** | Modular, highly configurable dynamic gaps for tiled and grid layouts. |

---

## 🛠️ Ecosystem & Tooling

* **Window Manager:** `dwm` (X11)
* **Status Bar:** `dwmblocks` (powered by custom bash utility scripts with Pango markup)
* **Application Launcher:** `dmenu` (custom-themed with storm-green maritime palettes)

---

## 📥 Installation & Compilation

Clone the repository and build from source:

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/yourusername/dwm-v1.git](https://github.com/yourusername/dwm-v1.git)
cd dwm-v1
sudo make clean install
